### ============================================================================================
### Weather images API  (VS Code "REST Client", Visual Studio .http editor, JetBrains HTTP Client)
###
### - deploy.ps1 rewrites the @baseUrl line below with the URL of your deployment.
### - Put the API key (printed by deploy.ps1, saved in .deploy/api-key.txt) in @apiKey.
### - Run the requests top to bottom: start a job, then poll the status, then fetch the images.
### ============================================================================================

# Azure:
@baseUrl = https://REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-FUNCTION-APP.azurewebsites.net/api
# Local (func start + Azurite):
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:7071/api

@apiKey = REPLACE-WITH-API-KEY


### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Start an image creation process
###    Needs the x-api-key header. Returns 202 Accepted + a unique job id immediately:
###    the work happens in the background via two Azure Storage queues.
###    Optional: ?count=10 (1-50, default 50; the Buienradar feed currently has 40 stations)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name startJob
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

###
### Same, but only 5 stations (faster to try out). The body variant { "count": 5 } works too.
# @name startSmallJob
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs?count=5
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Status / progress of the job
###    status: Queued -> Running -> Completed | CompletedWithErrors | Failed
###    Progress is read from Azure Table Storage (total / completed / failed / percentComplete).
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@jobId = {{startJob.response.body.$.jobId}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}


### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Results: links to every generated image (served from Blob Storage)
###    200 OK  when the job is finished,
###    202     while it is still running (with the images that are ready so far + Retry-After).
###    The links are read-only SAS URLs (private container); fetch the results again for fresh links.
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/images


### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Open one image: paste a "url" from the response above (it already contains its SAS token)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GET https://<storageaccount>.blob.core.windows.net/images/<jobId>/6275-arnhem.jpg?sv=...&sig=...


### ============================================================================================
### Error cases
### ============================================================================================

### Missing / wrong API key -> 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs

### Invalid count -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs?count=999
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Unknown job id -> 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/00000000000000000000000000000000

### Not a job id -> 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/not-a-guid/images
